WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.649
2008's The Strangers was a simple story of
a random home invasion that resonated with

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:07.120
audiences worldwide.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.019
While its box office performance warranted
a sequel, no one thought it would take nearly

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:12.540
ten years to happen.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.730
But now the Strangers have returned, and though
they may be in a new setting with a new cast,

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.020
the threat the invaders present remains the
same.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.680
The Strangers: Prey at Night follows a family
of four: parents Cindy and Mike, their son

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.140
Luke, and their daughter Kinsey.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:29.190
When they set off to visit relatives in a
countryside trailer park, their vacation turns

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.560
to terror when a trio of masked invaders descends
on the family with murder on their minds.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.390
Now that we're all safe at home, let's break
down the ending of The Strangers: Prey at

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.390
Night.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.720
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.430
The pool is closed
The climax of the movie kicks into high gear

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.330
once the parents are out of the picture, as
Kinsey and Luke set off to flee the trailer

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.330
park.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.970
But after a nasty encounter with Dollface,
Luke tells Kinsey to lay in hiding while he

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.280
sprints for help alone.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.620
He doesn't get very far.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.080
When he makes it to the trailer park's pool,
he comes face-to-face with the axe-wielding

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.200
Man in the Mask.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.870
Luke puts up a struggle, taking the fight
into the water, but he's overpowered, cut

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.230
up, and left to drown.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:08.869
It seems like things are over until two hands
burst into the water and pull him up — it's

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:12.260
Kinsey, back on her feet, there to save her
brother in the nick of time.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.329
With his wounds much more severe than hers,
the siblings switch places, as Luke hides

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:21.049
away while Kinsey makes a break for it, stumbling
into the street to a passing police officer,

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:24.700
who shows up so out of nowhere that Kinsey
can barely believe her eyes.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.109
As Kinsey falls into the arms of the officer,
neither of them notices the killer Dollface

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:30.529
approaching from behind.

00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:34.060
By the time that Kinsey sees her, it's too
late to do anything but watch the officer

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.619
get murdered.

00:01:35.619 --> 00:01:37.450
One shot, one kill

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:41.450
In one of the movie's most harrowing moments,
Kinsey tries to commandeer the police car

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.889
while Dollface overpowers her, pushing her
into the passenger seat as she stabs at her

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:46.889
over and over.

00:01:46.889 --> 00:01:49.490
But just when you think it's all over, Kinsey
gets tactical.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:50.490
Where is she?

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.729
A police car, and this one has a shotgun.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:56.549
The movie's most hopeless scene pivots to
its most triumphant moment as Kinsey grabs

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.890
the shotgun and executes Dollface with one
brutal blast to the head.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.889
I think we're alone now

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:07.290
After surviving another scrape, Kinsey tries
to start up the police car, while a truck

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.530
pulls up alongside Kinsey — it's the Man
in the Mask, of course.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.659
Both Strangers movies are notable for showcasing
the playful sadism of the killers.

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:18.680
Often, they get a chance to execute their
victims and just don't, preferring to terrify

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.090
and taunt their prey.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.060
"There's no reason why that's what's so horrible
about it."

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.600
"They found people that are awake, and they
thought it would be a fun thing to do.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.159
To torment them."

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:34.760
In the sequel, it's a tactic that works against
them, allowing their victims just enough chances

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.269
to get lucky, get away, or get revenge.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:41.459
This time, the Man in the Mask's taunt of
choice involves cranking the volume on Tiffany's

00:02:41.459 --> 00:02:42.480
"I Think We're Alone Now".

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.959
It's an on-the-nose choice.

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:48.200
"The music is great because you're screaming
you're crying and you've got this beautiful

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.349
music that like my mom grew up with and used
to be happy and pool parties and like summer

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:54.569
vacations playing over and over it."

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:56.349
Twisted metal

00:02:56.349 --> 00:03:01.079
The Man in the Mask backs up and smashes into
Kinsey's car until both vehicles explode into

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:02.079
flames.

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:05.820
Here, the ultimate stranger begins to appear
to be unkillable, surviving the explosion

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.189
to chase down Kinsey in his flaming truck
while she flees on foot.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:13.079
By then, the fire has burned off the man's
mask, but it's also burned away the flesh

00:03:13.079 --> 00:03:16.769
of his face, with the killer remaining anonymous
right down to the bone.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:20.620
This moment, as well as an earlier instance
where Kinsey declines an opportunity to remove

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.129
Dollface's mask, is sort of the whole point
of both films: They're monster movies that

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:26.680
don't have any monsters in them.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.450
The killers aren't Freddy Krueger — they're
just people, and they could be anybody.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:34.101
In the original, the killers removed their
masks off camera, making the point that their

00:03:34.101 --> 00:03:35.980
true identities don't matter.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.540
That's what makes them all so scary.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.310
If you survived an encounter like this, how
could you ever trust a stranger again?

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.420
"The thing that I love is I don't know who
the strangers are and I think they have absolutely

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.430
no reason to do it and that's what's scary."

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.890
The hitchhiker

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.889
Kinsey sticks to the road as she runs, pursued
on foot by the Man in the Mask, as a pickup

00:03:53.889 --> 00:03:55.109
truck approaches.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:58.290
Just as you start to think the encounter is
only going to up the killer's body count,

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.000
luck turns Kinsey's way again.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.180
She leaps into the back of the truck, screaming
as the burnt-up axeman grabs and swings at

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.180
her.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.249
The truck builds up speed, the killer loses
his grip… and Kinsey escapes.

00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:12.349
The ending is highly reminiscent of the conclusion
of The Texas Chainsaw Massacre, and just as

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:13.340
open-ended.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.420
While Texas Chainsaw cuts to credits at that
point, The Strangers: Prey at Night continues

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.470
— and that's when things get ambiguous.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.580
The bittersweet end

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:36.610
The movie ends on the reveal that Kinsey's
escape led to Luke's rescue, with the newly-orphaned

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.910
siblings reunited and alive in a dark hospital
room.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:43.470
Save for the machines, the room is silent
— until there's a knock at the door.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.500
Kinsey doesn't panic, but she's paralyzed.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.400
Someone's outside the door — a stranger.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.780
But is it really a killer?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.220
"You lock him out?"

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.230
"Mm-mmm."

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.760
The truth doesn't really matter.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.980
The ending is a metaphor for trauma, and the
lasting effects that a horrifying experience

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.350
can have on a person's psyche.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.720
What did her family do to deserve this torment?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:08.350
Nothing — and nothing they could have done
would have prevented it.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.460
"Why are you doing this to us?"

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:17.480
"Because you were home"
The fate of her family was tied to the whims

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:20.630
of three strangers — and at least one of
them could still be out there.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.100
The knock at the door is probably a nurse,
a doctor, a family friend.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.020
But after this experience, no matter what,
Kinsey can never put her trust in the kindness

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.240
of strangers again.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.820
Thanks for watching!

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:33.830
